e out  and you'll see the effect so let me  illustrate what would happen if you  could see it 10 hours later we keep this  going it starts off and it will  oscillate backwards and forwards with  this plane and now if you were to come  back say 10 hours later and it was still  going  you would see it with respect to the lab  moving in this direction  and if you come back even later it will  be moving in this plane and it will  continually rotate in its plane as time  progresses provided you can keep this  thing oscillating so i have here my  lovely demonstration of the north and  south pole so if we take this off and  imagine putting a pendulum here swinging  backwards and forwards at the north pole  because the earth is rotating i can't  remember which way it rotates you can  see as far as this pendulum is concerned  the earth is rotating underneath  my finger  and so the plane of this oscillation  remains constant  and this pendulum doesn't know that  there's the earth there apart from the  gravity that's pulling it down it has no  force pulling it in one direction or the  other  at this point and as far as it's  concerned it's just moving in a station  in an inertial frame that is a frame  which is stationary with respect to all  the moving stars around it and the earth  is moving  it will work at the poles and the period  of the pendulum  will be 24 hours because the earth  rotates roughly at 24 hours  if you come at the equator the earth is  not rotating about the equator it's not  rotating that way round it just going  around like that and there is no effect  at the equator if you come to let's say  great britain or france or even the  united states of america  then you have a latitude say of 45 50  degrees and the period of the pendulum  will go up to 32 or 33 hours so it  becomes longer and as you get towards  the equator the period gets towards  infinity and and when i talk about the  period what i don't mean is the period  of this pendulum going backwards and  forwards i mean the period which the  plane of this rotates around  what's happening is the earth is  imperceptibly moving under our feet  very slowly and you can't notice it and  why it was such a sensation foucault  demonstrated to people that they could  actually observe the rotation of the  earth  it's pretty cool isn't it  yeah i thought i was dead clever of fuco  i mean it's  it's something i wouldn't have thought  of and whenever i try and think about it  you have to have this idea that there  are stars out there which give you a  reference frame and the pendulum keeps  in a straight line with respect to the  stars but even that's not good enough i  talk to my friend and say all these  stars and galaxies are moving around and  then they say well when we're put in a  corner the astronomers say there's the  cosmic background radiation and if  you're in the right reference frame that  is isotropic in all directions  but  i just like the simple-minded  explanation
 

